window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2fea1dd9716dbca4"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-an-ai-tour-guide\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"ai\">构建 AI 导览助手</h1> <p>让用户在使用应用的过程中，通过会自适应的导览学会如何操作。</p> <p>使用 Codex 为 Web 应用加入 WebMCP 导览。高亮下一个控件、说明操作方式，并根据用户当前状态调整引导；由用户自己完成每一步。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>帮助新用户完成 Web 应用中第一个工作流程的团队。</li> <li>会因登录状态、已连接服务或已打开面板而改变的引导流程。</li> <li>希望用户自己学习控件并执行操作的任务。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建 AI 导览助手</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请为 [web app/repository]（Web 应用/代码库）添加一个引导式导览，让 Codex 可以展示用户如何完成 [complete one specific workflow]（某一个具体工作流程）。\n\n先阅读应用已有的 UI、状态管理和文档。使用 WebMCP 让 Codex 能够：\n- 通过稳定且有语义的 ID、标签和说明发现导览目标\n- 高亮某个目标并简短说明，然后取消高亮\n- 读取选择下一步所需的 UI 状态\n- 等待用户操作，再读取更新后的状态\n- 读取应用说明和相关文档\n\n用户应当自己完成整个工作流程。请将导览工具与实际执行操作的工具分开，并保留应用现有的身份验证与权限检查。\n\n从一条完整流程开始。复用现有组件和设计系统。在一个 Codex 能调用 WebMCP 工具的浏览器环境中测试导览，包括不同的起始状态、用户取消某一步，以及目标控件暂时不可见的情况。\n\n总结变更内容、验证结果和仍需完成的设置。未经我批准，不要部署或发布。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/blog/automating-repetitive-work-at-openai-with-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI 使用 Codex 自动处理重复工作（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://web.runme.dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runme（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b790d9afda421b3c\">使用 Computer Use 测试你的应用</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"introduction\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">简介</h2> <p>有些工作流程需要有人告诉你该去哪里、选择什么，才容易学会。你可以使用 Codex 构建导览，带领用户操作你的 Web 应用，同时让用户自己完成每个步骤。</p> <p>借助用于发现应用控件、状态和文档的 WebMCP 工具，Codex 可以根据用户当前看到的内容决定下一条说明。例如，尚未连接服务的用户与已完成设置的用户，需要从不同步骤开始。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>在 Codex 中打开应用代码库，选择一条要引导的工作流程，例如连接服务或添加文件夹。</li> <li>提供相关文档，并说明导览需要处理的起始状态。</li> <li>使用本页的起始提示词，添加导览目标、UI 状态工具，以及读取应用说明的能力。</li> <li>在 Codex 能调用应用 WebMCP 工具的浏览器环境中测试流程。让 Codex 引导你，再由你自己完成每一步。</li> </ol> <p>第一条导览应保持精简。先验证它能否带领用户从开始设置一直走到完成，再增加其他工作流程。</p> <p><a id=\"example-add-a-google-drive-folder-in-runme\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"runme-google-drive\">示例：在 Runme 中添加 Google Drive 文件夹</h2> <p>在 <a href=\"https://web.runme.dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runme（需联网）</a> 中，用户可以编辑 notebook，也可以通过文件浏览器添加 Google Drive 文件夹并浏览其中的文件。导览可以帮助新用户找到这些控件并学会操作流程。</p> <p>如需了解 Runme 的更多信息，可以阅读 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/blog/automating-repetitive-work-at-openai-with-codex.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI 使用 Codex 自动处理重复工作</a>。</p> <p>观看 Codex 高亮 Runme 的控件并说明其用途。下方截图展示的是一条独立、专注于添加 Google Drive 文件夹的导览。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">媒体内容 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/runme-ai-tour-demo.webm\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/runme-ai-tour-demo.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>Google Drive 导览从一条请求开始：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Show me how to add a Google Drive folder.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">演示如何添加一个 Google Drive 文件夹。</div></div> <p><a id=\"connect-google-drive\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"google-drive\">连接 Google Drive</h3> <p>Codex 会检查 Google Drive 是否已连接。如果尚未连接，Codex 会高亮显示 <strong>Connect Google Drive</strong>，并请用户选择它、完成连接。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex 在 Runme 中高亮显示 Connect Google Drive，并说明如何开始。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/connect-google-drive.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex 在 Runme 中高亮显示 Connect Google Drive，并说明如何开始。 · <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/connect-google-drive.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"open-the-file-explorer\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">打开文件浏览器</h3> <p>连接完成后，Codex 会引导用户找到文件浏览器。下一条说明会根据应用更新后的状态给出。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex 高亮显示用于打开 Runme 文件浏览器的控件。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/open-file-explorer.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex 高亮显示用于打开 Runme 文件浏览器的控件。 · <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/open-file-explorer.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"add-the-folder\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">添加文件夹</h3> <p>用户展开工具栏后，Codex 会高亮显示用于添加 Google Drive 文件夹的控件。用户始终掌控交互过程，也会学会下次从哪里找到这个控件。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex 高亮显示用于在 Runme 中添加 Google Drive 文件夹的控件。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/add-google-drive-folder.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex 高亮显示用于在 Runme 中添加 Google Drive 文件夹的控件。 · <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/add-google-drive-folder.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p><a id=\"give-codex-the-context-to-guide-users\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">为 Codex 提供引导用户所需的背景</h2> <p>Runme 的实现提供了三类背景信息：导览目标、应用状态和文档。下方的工具名来自 Runme；你可以将相同职责应用到自己的应用中。</p> <p><a id=\"make-controls-discoverable\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">让控件可以被发现</h3> <p>为每个导览目标设置稳定且有语义的 <code>data-tour-id</code> 值，并提供标签和说明。Runme 通过三个 WebMCP 工具暴露这些控件：</p> <ul> <li><code>listTargets</code>：列出已注册目标及其 ID、标签和说明。</li> <li><code>showTourStep({ target, title?, message, placement? })</code>：高亮目标并显示说明。</li> <li><code>dismiss</code>：移除高亮。</li> </ul> <p>这样，Codex 就能识别并说明控件，而不必代替用户执行对应操作。</p> <p><a id=\"read-state-and-wait-for-the-user\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">读取状态并等待用户操作</h3> <p>Runme 将导览相关状态保存在 React 之外，并通过控制器暴露。它的 <code>getUiSnapshot</code> 工具可以提供当前 UI 状态，包括登录状态。<code>waitForUiChange(...)</code> 则让 Codex 等待状态变化，例如用户选择了已高亮的控件。</p> <p>请让 Codex 在每次交互后重新读取状态。是否进入导览下一步，应取决于应用中实际发生了什么，而不应仅取决于 Codex 是否已经展示过一条说明。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-instructions-with-the-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">将说明与应用放在一起</h3> <p>Runme 将 Markdown 文档与应用打包，并通过 WebMCP 提供访问能力：</p> <ul> <li><code>readInstructionsForAIAgents</code>：说明 Codex 应如何与应用及其工具交互。</li> <li><code>listDocumentation()</code>：列出可用页面及其说明。</li> <li><code>getDocumentation({ name })</code>：以 Markdown 格式返回指定页面。</li> </ul> <p>导览说明和工具可以随应用一起交付，不需要另行创建 Codex 导览插件。</p> <p><a id=\"review-the-tour\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">审查导览</h2> <p>从不同的起始状态测试同一条请求。检查导览是否会跳过已完成的设置、等待用户操作，并在 UI 变化时更新引导内容。</p> <p>还要测试用户取消某一步，以及目标控件暂时不可见的情况。Codex 应说明缺少什么，或选择一个有效的下一步；不能仅仅因为高亮了按钮，就声称操作已经成功。</p> <p>保持身份验证、权限检查和用户操作处于应用现有流程中。导览的作用是帮助用户理解界面，而不是绕过这些控制措施。</p> <p><a id=\"good-follow-ups\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">后续可以尝试</h2> <p>第一条流程可用后，可以在同一对话中继续提出要求：</p> <ul> <li>“当 Google Drive 已连接、但文件浏览器关闭时，测试这条导览。”</li> <li>“处理用户取消某一步、随后要求继续导览的情况。”</li> <li>“复用现有目标和状态工具，为[下一条工作流程]添加导览。”</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-an-ai-tour-guide\">Build an AI tour guide</h1> <p>Help users learn your app with a tour that adapts as they go.</p> <p>Use Codex to add a WebMCP-powered tour to your web app. Highlight the next control, explain what to do, and adapt the guidance to the user's current state while they complete the steps themselves.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams helping new users complete their first workflow in a web app.</li> <li>Onboarding flows that change with sign-in status, connected services, or open panels.</li> <li>Tasks where users should learn the controls and perform the actions themselves.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build an AI tour guide</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Add a guided tour to [web app/repository] so Codex can show users how to [complete one specific workflow].\n\nRead the app's existing UI, state management, and documentation first. Use WebMCP to let Codex:\n- discover tour targets through stable, semantic IDs, labels, and descriptions\n- highlight a target with a short explanation and dismiss the highlight\n- read the UI state needed to choose the next step\n- wait for the user to act, then read the updated state\n- read the app's instructions and relevant documentation\n\nThe user should complete the workflow themselves. Keep tour tools separate from tools that perform actions, and preserve the app's existing authentication and permission checks.\n\nStart with one complete flow. Reuse the existing components and design system. Test the tour in a browser environment where Codex can call the WebMCP tools, including different starting states, a canceled step, and a target that isn't visible yet.\n\nSummarize what changed, what you verified, and any setup still needed. Do not deploy or publish without my approval.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/blog/automating-repetitive-work-at-openai-with-codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Automating repetitive work at OpenAI with Codex (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://web.runme.dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runme (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b790d9afda421b3c\">QA your app with Computer Use</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"introduction\">Introduction</h2> <p>Some workflows are easier to learn when someone shows you where to go and what to select. Use Codex to build a tour that guides users through your web app while they perform the actions themselves.</p> <p>With WebMCP tools for your app's controls, state, and documentation, Codex can choose the next instruction based on what the user sees. A user who hasn't connected a service needs a different first step from someone who has already completed setup.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Open your app's repository in Codex and choose one workflow to guide, such as connecting a service or adding a folder.</li> <li>Provide the relevant documentation and describe the starting states the tour should handle.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt on this page to add tour targets, UI-state tools, and access to the app's instructions.</li> <li>Test the flow in a browser environment where Codex can call your app's WebMCP tools. Ask Codex to guide you, then complete each step yourself.</li> </ol> <p>Keep the first tour narrow. Verify that it can guide a user from setup to completion before adding more workflows.</p> <h2 id=\"example-add-a-google-drive-folder-in-runme\">Example: Add a Google Drive folder in Runme</h2> <p>In <a href=\"https://web.runme.dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Runme (online)</a>, users edit notebooks and use a file explorer to add Google Drive folders and navigate their files. The tour helps a new user find those controls and learn the flow.</p> <p>To learn more about Runme, you can read <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/blog/automating-repetitive-work-at-openai-with-codex.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Automating repetitive work at OpenAI with Codex</a>.</p> <p>Watch Codex highlight Runme's controls and explain their purpose. The screenshots below show a separate, task-focused tour for adding a Google Drive folder.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">媒体内容 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/runme-ai-tour-demo.webm\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption><a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/runme-ai-tour-demo.webm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>The Google Drive tour starts with a request:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Show me how to add a Google Drive folder.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"connect-google-drive\">Connect Google Drive</h3> <p>Codex checks whether Google Drive is connected. If it isn't, Codex highlights <strong>Connect Google Drive</strong> and asks the user to select it and complete the connection.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex highlights Connect Google Drive in Runme and explains how to start. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/connect-google-drive.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex highlights Connect Google Drive in Runme and explains how to start. · <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/connect-google-drive.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"open-the-file-explorer\">Open the file explorer</h3> <p>After the connection is complete, Codex guides the user to the file explorer. The next instruction follows the updated app state.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex highlights the control for opening Runme&#x27;s file explorer. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/open-file-explorer.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex highlights the control for opening Runme's file explorer. · <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/open-file-explorer.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h3 id=\"add-the-folder\">Add the folder</h3> <p>Once the user expands the toolbar, Codex highlights the control for adding a Google Drive folder. The user stays in control of the interaction and learns where to find it next time.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">Codex highlights the control for adding a Google Drive folder in Runme. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/add-google-drive-folder.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>Codex highlights the control for adding a Google Drive folder in Runme. · <a href=\"https://cdn.openai.com/devhub/codex-use-cases/build-an-ai-tour-guide/add-google-drive-folder.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <h2 id=\"give-codex-the-context-to-guide-users\">Give Codex the context to guide users</h2> <p>Runme's implementation provides three kinds of context: tour targets, application state, and documentation. The tool names below come from Runme; adapt the same roles to your app.</p> <h3 id=\"make-controls-discoverable\">Make controls discoverable</h3> <p>Give tour targets stable, semantic <code>data-tour-id</code> values, with a label and description for each. Runme exposes these controls through three WebMCP tools:</p> <ul> <li><code>listTargets</code> lists the registered targets, IDs, labels, and descriptions.</li> <li><code>showTourStep({ target, title?, message, placement? })</code> highlights a target and displays an explanation.</li> <li><code>dismiss</code> removes the highlight.</li> </ul> <p>This gives Codex a way to identify and explain a control without performing its action for the user.</p> <h3 id=\"read-state-and-wait-for-the-user\">Read state and wait for the user</h3> <p>Runme keeps tour-related state outside React and exposes it through a controller. Its <code>getUiSnapshot</code> tool provides the current UI state, including sign-in status. <code>waitForUiChange(...)</code> lets Codex wait for a change, such as the user selecting the highlighted control.</p> <p>Ask Codex to read the state again after each interaction. Advancing the tour should depend on what happened in the app, not on whether Codex has already shown an instruction.</p> <h3 id=\"keep-instructions-with-the-app\">Keep instructions with the app</h3> <p>Runme bundles Markdown documentation with the application and makes it available through WebMCP:</p> <ul> <li><code>readInstructionsForAIAgents</code> explains how Codex should interact with the app and its tools.</li> <li><code>listDocumentation()</code> lists the available pages and their descriptions.</li> <li><code>getDocumentation({ name })</code> returns a selected page as Markdown.</li> </ul> <p>The tour instructions and tools can ship with the app, without a separate Codex plugin for the tour.</p> <h2 id=\"review-the-tour\">Review the tour</h2> <p>Try the same request from different starting states. Check that the tour skips completed setup, waits for the user, and updates its guidance when the UI changes.</p> <p>Also test a canceled step and a control that isn't visible yet. Codex should explain what is missing or choose a valid next step. It shouldn't claim that an action succeeded just because it highlighted a button.</p> <p>Keep authentication, permission checks, and user actions in the existing app flow. The tour should help users understand the interface without bypassing those controls.</p> <h2 id=\"good-follow-ups\">Good follow-ups</h2> <p>Once the first flow works, continue in the same chat:</p> <ul> <li>\"Test this tour when Google Drive is already connected and the file explorer is closed.\"</li> <li>\"Handle a user canceling a step, then asking to continue the tour.\"</li> <li>\"Add a tour for [next workflow], reusing the existing targets and state tools.\"</li> </ul>"};
